{"amendments":[{"body":"`crates/tank_tui/src/lib.rs:234-240` still loads on-disk saves with `serde_json::from_str::<SaveFile>()`, while the new schema checks and migration chain only run in `SaveFile::from_json` / `SaveFile::from_value` (`crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:86-176`). This means the TUI file-load path can still bypass version validation and migrations: a legacy save can fail before migration once a new required field is added, and a v2 save that omitted `stability_tracker` will be deserialized with default zeros and then reserialized back to the API instead of getting the reseeded baseline that `from_json` applies. Route disk loads through the migration-aware constructor, or make `SaveFile`'s `Deserialize` impl delegate to that path so every consumer gets the same behavior.","rationale":"The task's save-compatibility contract is only enforced on some load paths today; the existing TUI path can still reject valid old saves or silently alter migrated state."}],"summary":"Reviewed the save-schema migration changes, related tests, and load callers. The migration registry and tests look reasonable, but I found one correctness gap: the TUI's local file-load path still bypasses the new migration/versioning logic."}